   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tripartite partners have developed an Alternative Dispute Resolution mechanism, cantered around mediation with the formation of a pool of mediators, promoting effective labour dispute prevention and resolution. The proposed ADR mechanism was developed following a mapping which revealed a gap in established dispute resolution mechanisms, particularly relating to individual dispute resolution. The ILO conducted a comprehensive mapping on the existing Labour dispute mechanisms in 2022, with a thorough analysis of related regulations. In addition, the ILO provided necessary technical specialist expertise for the development of the ADR as well as the action plan. Moreover, the ILO provided capacity building to tripartite partners on labour dispute prevention and resolution creating a pool of mediators for any foreseen ADR mechanism.</narrative>
   </description>
